reviews.review:
Pros:
- millions of quests;
- a large amount of weapons, many of them are interesting, although each weapon class has its obvious leaders;
- good MACO, at last;
- interesting, different, various, and cool worlds;
- co-op multiplayer (I'm the Warframe fan, but Andromeda's co-op I like much more);
- convenient character leveling, and a variety of classes pleases;
- the combat system is much better than in ME 1-3.

Cons
- millions of semi-identical quests (go and kill someone or bring something);
- boring personal quests of party members;
- unfinished main story, and in the foreseeable future, we won't see the continuation of the story;
- co-op seems unfinished: few maps, opponents, no variety of goals, because of this the multiplayer is almost dead;
- from planet to planet the enemies mostly are identical;
- animations (face, run, turn, walk, etc.) still ♥♥♥♥♥♥ up, after all these years;
- Just simply incredible, monstrous amount of completely meaningless flights from planet to planet and transitions from location to location. To talk to a companion who is nearby, right here, on the ship, you HAVE to fly to some kind of ♥♥♥♥♥ bar! Seriously?! You have to cross half the galaxy for the companion to say "I approve!" on some hole in the balcony? Dear players, if you want to play the cheap version of Death Stranding, if you want to feel like a courier, then here it is, a perfect game!
- stupid and boring sex scenes. Bioware, come on! That's your games' bread and butter! Why have you failed SO hard?!

===

Summary:

If you are waiting for a good story, wonderful cinematic cutscenes, deep characters (at least some of these characters), interesting quests, Miranda's ass... Well, abort this game.

BUT.

If you want to see interesting worlds, gather different junk and craft, oh well, junk, and have fun from fights and stupid scenes in good ol' Star Track style, then, definitely, you should try it. I'm into this ♥♥♥♥, so that's why I approve (!) this game.

And I hope, Bioware won't continue the game developement like this. It's just a shame when the game is made for the sake of the plot and exploring, but its main advantage is the shooting element in nearly dead co-op. If Bioware will turn Andromeda into Doom: Eternal or Warframe, I will be pleased. Because, it seems, they can't turn the game into Mass Effect.
